WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:05.190
Black Panther has brought to life a new chapter
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe that's refreshing,

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.220
innovative, and full of compelling characters.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.160
It also helps pave the way for Marvel's next
on-screen adventure with Avengers: Infinity

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.160
War in a few key ways.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:18.180
Let's take a look at how Black Panther sets
the stage for the third Avengers extravaganza.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.000
A new smartie

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.230
The MCU is built upon a sturdy foundation
of super-geniuses, including Tony Stark and

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.710
Bruce Banner, two men of science who are responsible
for much of the technology and innovation

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.040
that makes the super-heroics of Marvel possible.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:36.620
Heck, Tony's dad Howard is another great Marvel
genius, and one of the men responsible for

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.400
the creation of Captain America.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.460
In the wake of Black Panther, though, there's
a new smartest kid on the block… and we

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.360
mean "kid" in the most literal sense.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.920
Shuri, T'Challa's 16-year-old sister, has
now been established as the smartest person

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.700
in the MCU, which means she'll have the edge
on innovation from here on out.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:53.740
And who knows.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:58.160
Maybe she'll get to cross paths with Peter
Parker, the other teen genius of the MCU.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:00:59.980
"Whoo!

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:00.500
Let's go!"

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.080
A new shield

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:06.860
Captain America's original shield was forged
from vibranium, which meant it could withstand

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.400
bullets, explosions, and everything else his
foes threw at him.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:14.840
But at the end of Civil War, Tony Stark demanded
he return the shield that his father had designed,

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.940
and it's unlikely he'll pick it back up before
the Infinity War.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:22.819
However, since he's taken refuge in Wakanda,
T'Challa is going to be pinching off another

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.580
piece of vibranium to make Cap a new shield
before the big battle begins.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.620
"And get this man a shield."

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.760
And from the looks of the Infinity War's trailer,
he's gonna like it.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:33.300
"Let's go."

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.160
Bucky is back

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.960
One of the other significant cliffhangers
at the end of Civil War is the fate of Bucky

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.660
Barnes, the former Winter Soldier and Cap's
best friend.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:47.430
While he's begun to remember his past after
being brainwashed by Hydra, some of his programming

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.140
still remains.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:52.400
The film ends with him going into cryogenic
slumber to wait it out while a cure is developed.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.580
Black Panther's second post-credits scene
provides some resolution with the revelation

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:02.040
that Bucky is back — only now he's going
by Shuri's nickname for him, "White Wolf."

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.380
Considering he's shown sporting a new arm
in the teasers for Infinity War, there's a

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.280
good chance he'll have Shuri to thank for
the spiffy prosthesis.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.140
The Soul Stone

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.060
Most of the Infinity Stones have been found
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe so far, except

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:17.300
for the Soul Stone.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:21.920
With Black Panther marking the last film before
Infinity War, many have drawn the conclusion

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.560
that the Soul Stone may be hiding away in
Wakanda.

00:02:25.049 --> 00:02:29.019
It's been suggested that the stone may lie
in the heart of the massive vibranium deposit

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:32.200
under Wakanda, granting the metal its multitude
of special abilities.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:36.620
From the previews, it looks like Thanos is
going to pay the once-hidden nation a visit

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.480
in Infinity War, so what else would bring
him into town but the bauble he's been after?

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:42.560
Ready to fight

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:48.500
Between its various tribes, the Dora Milajae,
and Black Panther himself, Wakanda is a military

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.480
force to be reckoned with.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:54.409
Its policy of isolation has kept it from war
with the outside world, so we've yet to see

00:02:54.409 --> 00:02:56.500
what a collective Wakanda would look like
in battle.

00:02:57.049 --> 00:03:00.579
The film's climax gave us a peek at this,
but even then we were only seeing a couple

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.120
of tribes and the Dora Milajae.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:07.820
Of course, the trailers for Infinity War have
given us some hint as to how massive a full-scale

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:08.840
Wakandan army might be.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:13.400
And in the wake of Black Panther, the nation's
policy of isolationism has ended, so they'll

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.720
now be sharing their technology and resources
with the world, which means Earth's defenses

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.660
just got a lot more promising.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:24.390
The Wakandan weaponry in Black Panther is
shown to be second to none, heavily utilizing

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:27.340
vibranium and the technology Shuri and her
team have built around it.

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:32.000
With an entire lab full of toys Shuri has
designed, and an alien invasion coming their

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:36.659
way, Wakandan vibranium weaponry will be a
must for the team and may end up being the

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:39.280
only reason our heroes stand a chance against
Thanos.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.220
A new team leader

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.640
One of the cool things about the MCU's Avengers
is that they really do seem to function as

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.000
a sort of miniature democracy.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:52.260
Of course, that team dynamic has significantly
shifted in the wake of Civil War, and it looks

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.140
like Infinity War will bring even more changes
to the group.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:59.440
One seems all but certain: If T'Challa joins
the Avengers, there may be a new sheriff in

00:03:59.440 --> 00:03:59.940
town.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.420
It's not that T'Challa will install himself
as the team's benevolent dictator or anything,

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:08.960
but more likely, since he's a literal king,
he probably isn't going to be taking a subordinate

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.560
position as an Avenger.

00:04:10.889 --> 00:04:14.600
It seems far more likely that we'll see him
step up and take on the responsibility of

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.500
leadership for the new Avenger refugees.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:18.500
And who knows?

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.760
Maybe he and Iron Man will become equals in
head honcho status.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.780
Either way, don't expect him to be relegated
to coffee runs.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.220
Thanks for watching!

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.540
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:31.260
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

